        // position — the in-block copath (8 levels, a constant of the cover shape) and the block roots to
        // fold — instead of paging the entire note stream to rebuild a depth-32 path.
        //
        // The binder is THIS spend's nullifier, so the commitment it yields is exactly the one the spend
        // carrier above welded in-circuit: the two proofs are one claim about one note.
        //
        // Attached only when the wallet knows where the note sits (the account-bucket lookup tells it). A
        // note whose position is unknown carries no membership proof and is authorised the existing way —
        // this ADDS evidence, it never substitutes for the spend's own anchor, so nothing here can make an
        // unauthorised spend pass.
        // ⭐ §19 (2026-10-28): NO ONE-STEP BIND — it named the RECORD holding the spent note (`PqTx::membership_tip`, filed
        // open as a spend-to-receive join). The member leg below (DB-223 Q7, on every send) is the membership evidence
        // the node admits; a node that cannot vouch for its anchor answers a retry, never an admission.
        let (membership_carrier_hex, membership_tip_hex) = (String::new(), String::new());
        // ⭐ CONSTANT-WIDTH OWNED CARRY. The decoy seed is keyed by the owner's NULLIFIER KEY (`nk`) — wallet-only
        // material (DB-395: the note's payer holds its seed and opening, never `nk`) — so no observer and no payer can
        // recompute the decoys and pick the real spend out of them. The nullifier only makes it unique per note.
        let tx_secret = tx_cover_secret(&owner.nk, &nfb);
        // ⛔⛔⛔ THE PER-BLOCK ABSENCE FOLD IS OFF THE SEND PATH — IT WAS THE TIME GROWTH.
        //
        // user 2026-08-09: *"time growth on sends is unacceptable... No blockchain has sends that take
        // longer as the chain grows."*
        //
        // `build_fold_absence_carry` folded `base..tip` on EVERY send. MEASURED on the live pair:
        // `[absence] folded 27 blocks in 1.14s (42ms/block)` and later `30 blocks in 2.89s (96ms/block)` —
        // 1.2-2.9s of a ~4s send, rising with chain length forever. Making it faster was the wrong move; it
        // had to leave the money path.
        //
        // The deletion transition already carried in `unspent_spends_hex` is the authority now: the node
        // checks `fold(cm, copath) == old_root` / `fold(EMPTY, copath) == new_root` against its ONE live
        // root in FIXED work at any height, and a re-spend finds EMPTY and fails closed with no history
        // consulted. "`cm` was in the tree at root R" is immutable, so nothing decays and nothing needs
        // refreshing between building a spend and its landing.
        //
        // The padded nullifier set is still built and still carried — only the recursive per-block fold is
        // gone. An absence proof, if one is ever carried again, is still verified by the node and a forged
        // one still rejects; this removes a REQUIREMENT, never a check.
        // ⭐⭐⭐ THE SPEND AUTHORITY, ATTACHED — AND BUILT SOMEWHERE ELSE.
