        // ⛔⛔⛔ WHAT THIS REPLACES: `let absence_hex = String::new();`. The comment above explains why the
        // per-block fold left the send path, and that was right — but the field was then left EMPTY and
        // nothing took over, so every wallet-originated spend arrived at a door whose own words are *"the
        // recursive carrier is the SOLE spend authority … so nothing can settle without it"* and was
        // answered `[nf-gate] REJECT: N input(s) carried NO absence proof`. The deletion transition named
        // above as "the authority now" was retired with the unspent tree (Z1), which left this send with
        // no authority at all. The 0.00 balance was the same hole seen from the display side.
