        // send shipped `built` — the witness taken when it STARTED, stale by the whole prove — to a door that
        // admits only `claimed_tip == live`. The witness that travels is now read at the tip (see the encode
        // below), and a carrier that cannot stand there fails the send CLOSED with its real state instead of
        // shipping a proof the door refuses.
        // ROOT-LAYER: the witness is PRODUCED by the carrier follower; this is the one read that decides which
        // witness travels, so it waits on the producer's progress instead of substituting an older value.
        // MEASURED: real node pairs 2026-09-26, 3 of 3 runs on both builds — sends of 3.8 s … 68.7 s ALL refused
        // by the absence door; the after-number is the send probe's node log.
        // MUST-STAY-GREEN: a note whose carrier cannot stand on the tip is reported UNSPENT and untouched with a
        // retry, exactly as the early read reports it; the wallet lib suite.
        // ⛔ DB-329 §7f (lane stable 2026-11-01): row 1 is witnessed over the pair whose image IS `t1` — the carrier's own
        // claim: `(slot_key, d)` for a slot CLAIM (`build_spend_validity_carrier_self_claiming`), `(lc_blind, 0)` for every
        // other send (`ordinary_claim_tag`). This always named the ordinary pair, so every claim's proof witnessed a tag
        // its row does not carry and failed: MEASURED (stable/pa6.log, the post-adopt journey PA.4) "[device-slot] the
        // self-claim of slot 1 was not sent this pass (could not prove the constant-width tag set (spend-or-decoy))" — a
        // seed restored on a second device could never claim its slot, so it could never send.
