        // (the padded set, the cover secret, `nk`, the leaf, the claim pair) are all in hand; joined before the submit body.
        // MEASURED (`[send-phases]`, fast journeys on 2fad4da): with only the validity prove beside, the rest of the send was
        // 5.2–16.8 s in sequence (evidence fetch → this prove → member refresh + member prove).
        let decoy_job = {
            let (padded, secret, nk) = (padded_nfs.clone(), tx_secret, spent_key);
            std::thread::spawn(move || {
                let t0 = Instant::now();
                (build_spend_or_decoy_proof(&padded, &secret, nk, my_leaf, claim_pair), t0.elapsed().as_millis())
            })
        };
        // ⭐⭐⭐ CARRY THE NON-MEMBERSHIP WITNESS — THE SPENDER'S HALF OF THE MINA SPLIT.
        //
        // user 2026-07-30: *"lets make the spender hold its own witness"*.
        //
        // MEASURED, the exact live blocker: `[nf-gate] witness source for input 0: local-index-fallback
        // (carried=0 of 32 inputs)`. `PqTx.nullifier_witnesses` existed, the RPC parsed
        // `nullifier_witnesses_hex` into it, and the node's gate prefers it — but this send never sent the
        // field, so the node fell back to a local sparse index that would need ~38 MILLION nodes at this
        // height to answer. An UNSPENT tag then reads SPENT, and honest money is refused.
        //
        // One constant-shaped fetch for the FULL padded width (reals indistinguishable from decoys), then
        // shipped verbatim. The node re-folds each copath against its own root, so this is data we supply, not
        // trust we ask for: a wrong witness fails the same check on either side.
        // ⛔⛔⛔ DO NOT SWALLOW THE NODE'S ANSWER AT THE RPC BOUNDARY. `.ok()` turns EVERY non-2xx into `None`
        // and `unwrap_or_default()` turns that into an empty witness string — so when the node answers
